shadowfetch-control-center (2.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New package: the Control Center becomes its own deb and grows the
    "Fire Edition" shell. Takes over /usr/bin/shadowfetch-control from
    shadowfetch-defaults (Replaces:); the six 2.1.1 action cards all
    survive inside their new sections, so nothing users could reach
    before is gone.
  * Six fixed sidebar sections: Ignite, Watch, Recover, Agents, Drivers,
    and "Software & Updates" (subtitle "Updates & bundles") - named so the
    release's headline safety feature is never hidden behind a word that
    means "app store".
  * Deep links: --page section[:tab][:point=N], with single-instance
    routing over the session bus (com.shadowfetch.ControlCenter). A second
    launch fronts the existing window instead of opening another, so every
    entry point - Welcome, the Firewatch empty state, the Phoenix overlay
    banner, Fireproof notifications - lands in one window.
  * Ignite: the Ember switch with the safety promise on the card BEFORE
    the flip ("Always returns to Balanced automatically - safe to try"),
    the three-state flame driven by Firewatch's flame level, a readout
    strip bound to Firewatch (emberd has no sampler), a duration picker
    that goes through the shadowfetch-ember pkexec helper, and the
    two-card app-profile row (Gaming with live GameMode status, Local AI
    with the hardware verdict). Profiles are presets of Ember - the row
    header says exactly that.
  * Watch: sensor tiles that say "sensor not available" instead of
    guessing, the heat map with humanized names and icons resolved by the
    daemon (the UI never sees a cgroup path), PSS labelled where shown,
    the "resource heat, not temperature" note, and a Models tab whose
    empty state deep-links the Welcome AI catalog. When firewatchd is down
    the page says so and shows no stale numbers.
  * Recover: Phoenix Points listed via snapperd's D-Bus, restore through
    pkexec phoenix-restore (works from inside a "Last Known Good Flame"
    overlay session, with the Point preselected), the 1:1
    DISABLE_APT_SNAPSHOT toggle, the honest ext4 banner, and the repair
    toolkit (sources repair, driver reinstall, desktop reset with a
    timestamped backup, recovery report, text-mode recovery menu).
  * Agents, Drivers, Software & Updates: hardware verdicts from the local
    fact file with their scan timestamp, VRAM always labelled with its
    source, "may need firmware" wording for Wi-Fi (never "broken"),
    bundles rendered from the same catalog records Welcome uses and
    installed through the same id-locked pkexec helper, and the only
    permitted sidebar badge (pending updates from fireproofd).
  * Session-side Ember helper: suspends Baloo indexing at login when
    Ember is already active, covering re-login during an Ember run.
  * No telemetry, no network connections: every number on screen comes
    from a local bus, a local file, or a local command, and the page says
    so in plain words when a source cannot answer.

 -- Shadowfetch Project <signing@shadowfetch.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0400
